  "schemaVersion": 20,
  "description": "Vertical railway (Phase 4.5 Stage S4). Node heights are z in world units (64 a metre), within 4096 of the ground (0). An edge's height follows its chainage: with no transitions one grade, R*s/L; with vertical curves T0 and T1, D = 2L - T0 - T1 and R*s^2/(T0*D), R*(2s - T0)/D, R*(T1*D - (L-s)^2)/(T1*D), each rounded half up. The steepest grade is 2R/D, at most 40 in 1000. Surface track stays within 128 of the ground, viaducts and bridges at or above it, tunnels at or below it; track costs 1, 3, 4 or 5 times the track price a tile. The ramp 1 (0 to 512 over 12800) is exactly 1 in 25; 513 is too steep. The eased ramp 2 (512 over 16384, curves of 2048) is 9 high 1024 along, 256 in the middle and 503 1024 from the end, 1 in 56 and 1 in 28. Where tracks meet in plan away from a shared node, one must be at least 512 above the other: surface track under ramp 1 (246 there) is refused; the tunnel at -512 passes 758 below it and 695 below ramp 2 (183 there), and surface track exactly 512 above the tunnel is allowed. Node 11 is a tunnel portal. Station Deep has a platform 1024 to 5120 along the level tunnel 6, at -512; platforms belong to the railway network, and their ends cut the edge's spans, but these two already fall on boundaries of edge 6 (7168, seven spans of 1024). Mole (3 cars) stands 1024 into the falling tunnel (-41) with its body over the portal, runs 15 minutes at 1000 to 3224 along the platform tunnel, whole along the platform, and turns round. High on ramp 1 at (8192, 4096, 246) stands right over Low in the tunnel at -512: they share no resource. Resources are nodes and spans of edges (Stage S3A): edges 1 and 5 (12800) are 13 spans, with boundaries at floor(k * 12800 / 13): 984, 1969, 2953, 3938, 4923, 5907, 6892 and on; edge 4 (4096) is four spans of 1024. Mole placed with its tail at 3072 on edge 4 touches a boundary and holds both spans there; at 3024 on edge 5 it covers 976 to 3024, four spans; High at 6144 holds 5907-6892.",
